Firmware and factory data
-------------------------

Qualcomm, Xiaomi and Cirrus firmware remain subject to their respective
licenses. Inclusion in a download bundle does not place firmware under MIT.
Redistribution permissions and notices must be established for each distributed
firmware set before publication.

Device-specific calibration, WLAN and Bluetooth addresses and factory sensor
registry data are read from the user's tablet. They are not public source or
shared firmware assets and must not be distributed.

Fingerprint integration
-----------------------

Optional device/fingerprint/oem source retains file-level BSD-2-Clause,
LGPL-2.1-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later and Apache-2.0 notices. QSEE supplicant/QCBOR
retain upstream BSD licenses. QSEE supplicant is by Dawid Wróbel
(https://github.com/wrobelda/qsee-supplicant); QCBOR is by Laurence Lundblade
(https://github.com/laurencelundblade/QCBOR). Exact dependencies are in
device/fingerprint/oem/SOURCE_LOCK.json.
The fprintd original source remains external and hash-pinned; distribution of
binaries must include corresponding source/adaptation as required by its license.
OEM TA firmware, credentials, HATs, templates, raw images and private calibration
are not included in this source repository.

Release notification helper and offline tests: imported from
https://github.com/yzddmr6/xiaomipad-8pro-mainline
(MIT; shared mainline-release-notifier implementation). Project identity is
adapted for Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro; notification never installs an update.

Firefox for the Ubuntu desktop image

Mozilla distributes the unmodified arm64 Firefox deb and archive signing key
at https://packages.mozilla.org/apt. Firefox carries MPL-2.0 and the licenses
of its bundled libraries. The image builder records the package URL and SHA256.
The APT policy and profile-preserving snap migration are adapted from
https://github.com/yzddmr6/xiaomipad-8pro-mainline at 0cc2cc9
and its credited OnePlus implementation. Source headers are retained.
